Q: Refresh progress bar A: <p><strong>BackgroundWorker</strong> is clean and legible:</p>

<pre><code>var bw = new BackgroundWorker();

bw.DoWork += (s, e) =&gt;
{
    var worker = s as BackgroundWorker;
    Method1();
    worker.ReportProgress(30);
    Method2();
    worker.ReportProgress(80);
    Method3();
    worker.ReportProgress(100);
};

bw.ProgressChanged += (s, e) =&gt;
{
    pb.Value += e.ProgressPercentage;
};

bw.RunWorkerCompleted += (s, e) =&gt; 
{ 
};

bw.RunWorkerAsync();
</code></pre>

Q: Switch to minimize some icons on page A: <p>Toggle a <code>dataset</code> (<code>data-*</code> attribute) on a parent element (I'll use <code>body</code> in the example below), and style accordingly using CSS:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const el = (sel, par = document) =&gt; par.querySelector(sel);
const sizeToggle = () =&gt; el('body').dataset.tog = el('body').dataset.tog !== "true";
el('#size-toggle').addEventListener('click', sizeToggle);</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.sizeable {
  transition: zoom 0.5s;
  [data-tog=true] &amp; { zoom: 0.5; }
}

#size-toggle {
  span + span { display: none; }
  [data-tog=true] &amp; span  { display: none; &amp; + span { display: initial; } }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button id="size-toggle"&gt;
  Make Images &lt;span&gt;Smaller&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Larger&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img class="sizeable" src="//placehold.co/100x50/0bf/png" alt="Sample Image"&gt;
&lt;img class="sizeable" src="//placehold.co/100x50/fb0/png" alt="Sample Image"&gt;
&lt;img class="sizeable" src="//placehold.co/100x50/f0b/png" alt="Sample Image"&gt;</code></pre>
